33,90,66,92,284,1124,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,19,24984,220,22,24984,220,17,1124,408,90,5187,2555,2137,1124,31610,1124,10374,13233,90,65,92,1124,15136,1124,10374,13233,90,66,92,284,1124,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,16,24984,481,22,24984,220,16,23,1124,408,90,5187,2555,92,7110,60,46254,57960,10374,13233,90,66,92,1124,15136,320,18,1124,10374,13233,90,64,92,481,220,17,1124,10374,13233,90,65,16630,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c}$ be three vectors such that\n\\[\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]Compute $\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"ac5ef49306d7444461100232753035309998368e5c52da3dfc79255650337bae"},"seconds":18.048896551132202,"seed":842738627815323077,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for \\(\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b})\\), we will use the distributive property of the cross product, which states that for any vectors \\(\\mathbf{u}\\), \\(\\mathbf{v}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{w}\\), and any scalars \\(m\\) and \\(n\\), we have \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times (m\\mathbf{v} + n\\mathbf{w}) = m(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}) + n(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{w})\\). Applying this property, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}) = 3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) - 2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}).\n\\]\n\nWe are given \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}\\), so \\(\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a} = -\\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\). We are also given \\(\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix}\\). Substituting these into the expression, we get:\n\n\\[\n3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) - 2 (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}) = 3 \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} - 2 \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the scalar multiplications and the vector subtraction:\n\n\\[\n3 \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix},\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 36 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nSubtracting these vectors, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 - 2 \\\\ -21 - (-14) \\\\ -6 - 36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -14 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -42 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -14 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -42 \\end{pmatrix}}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -14 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -42 \\end{pmatrix}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"precalculus:429"}
